\newlabel{sec:ablation}{{5.5}{8}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{fig:inference-time}{{5}{9}{\textbf  {Inference Time Comparison:} The plot illustrates the tradeoff between RMSE and inference time. RDDM demonstrates the best balance across all datasets, outperforming DDPM with (T$=50$) even though the latter is approx. $2.5 \times $ slower, highlighting the efficiency and effectiveness of the proposed method. }{}{}}
\newlabel{fig:ablation}{{6}{9}{ \textbf  {Left:} RDDM shows an improvement in performance when $\Gamma $ is increased from $16$ to $32$, but beyond that, the performance degrades. \textbf  {Right:} On both datasets, RDDM achieves the best performance in just $10$ sampling steps. }{}{}}
